```
When the test gets executed, it will try to set some value at a specific index and then check if conditions get satisfied or not. If not, the Assertions in the contract (as Trace.Assert in this case) get executed and the unit test will break, indicating a failure in the contract.
```C#
    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ index passed in is less than or equal to last index of x in new array 
    Trace.Assert(Old_index <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ x in new array is different from old x
    Trace.Assert(x != Old_x);
```
### PexParameterAttributeContractTest 
```C#
[ContractTestClass]
public partial class PexParameterAttributeContractTest
{
    [ContractTestMethod]
    [PexMethod(typeof(int), "PUT_SetContract")]
    [PexCustomAttribute(typeof(PexAssumeUnderTestAttribute), typeof(ArrayList), "testArrayList", AllowMultiple = true)]
    [PexCustomAttribute(typeof(PexAssumeUnderTestAttribute), typeof(int), "x", AllowMultiple = true)]
    [PexCustomAttribute(typeof(PexAssumeUnderTestAttribute), typeof(int), "index", AllowMultiple = true)]
    public void PutSetContract(ArrayList testArrayList, int x, int index)
    {
        PexAssume.IsTrue(index >= 0 && index < testArrayList.Count);
        testArrayList[index] = x;
    }
}
```
In our PexParameterAttributeContractTest class, we marked all methods as ContractTestMethods using the attribute [ContractTestMethod]. For those methods, we passed into the method some dummy parameters and then we made sure that it contains assumptions (conditions that our method should satisfy), otherwise the method won't be executed.--------------------            Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX > index);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ index passed in or x has been changed to x in new array 
            Assert(New_arrListContainsX == true && New_arrListLastIndexOfX == index);

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ count passed in or x has been changed to x in new array 
            Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount);

	    // an invariant that @@@ all elements in the array from index 0 to the index before where the value has been set should be the same in the old array
            for (int i = 0; i<index; i++)
            {
                Assert(arrList[i] == Old_arrListCount);
            }
        }
    }
}--------------------
